  "summary": {
    "plain": "A longer IGEX run improved the limit: for the first time a germanium experiment cut into the region where DAMA's signal would lie, using raw data only.",
    "technical": "40 days of data from one IGEX detector (threshold about 4 keV): spin-independent WIMP-nucleon exclusion plot improving all other germanium ionization limits from 20 to 200 GeV and excluding the upper left part of the DAMA region."
